Description: Dodo desktop session: labwc, Waybar and xfdesktop defaults
 The Dodo desktop as a login session: labwc with the Dodo theme,
 key and mouse bindings and an English menu, a two-bar Waybar panel,
 desktop icons and wallpaper from xfdesktop, and systemd user units that
 start and stop them with the session.
 .
 Defaults live in /usr/share/dodo/xdg and are found through
 XDG_CONFIG_DIRS, so apt upgrades them and a user's own ~/.config always
 wins. Per-machine settings (primary monitor, a monitor pinned to every
 desktop) go in /etc/dodo/session.conf; the package names no monitor.
 .
 Rounded corners and shadows need the Dodobian build of labwc, and icons on
 the primary monitor the Dodobian build of libxfce4windowing; with Debian's
 builds the session still works and says so in its log.
